32,2,1,talk,Mio,,"It looks like we have a bit of a bottleneck with our people. Our recruiters are great for support roles, but finding field crews or supervisors is taking forever, and our software board seats are totally full.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,George,,"Interestingly, our most successful exits were quiet back-office financial tools. On the other hand, the one we wrote off involved physical premises and hourly staff. Retention is also stronger for field instruments and medical practices.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,May,,"Our liquidity is tighter than it looks. Follow-on calls are happening twice as fast as we modeled, and our credit line is useless for anything other than stock—subscriptions and invoices don't count as security.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,1,talk,Rin,,"I found out that things with depots or hardware make our audits way longer and more expensive! Also, we can only independently verify figures for holdings with field instruments or moving goods.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"It seems we have a pattern of delays. Security reviews for medical or financial data take three times longer than others, and hardware assembly has caused significant setbacks, whereas bank-integrated software has been seamless.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@George, that's a really interesting point about the back-office tools. If we're already full on software board seats, though, can we even afford to take on another one?","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,George,,"That is a fair question, Mio. However, the data suggests that the software tools—specifically the quiet, back-office ones—are where our actual returns are coming from, regardless of our current board capacity.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,May,,"@Mizuki, if we're struggling with liquidity and the credit line only favors stock, we should be very careful about any candidate that requires heavy physical assets or constant follow-on funding.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@May, that matches what I found! Hardware and depots make our audits a nightmare and cost us a lot more. We should definitely avoid anything that makes the quarter-end more stressful.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Rin, exactly. Between the audit delays and the security review times for sensitive data, we need to be very mindful of the operational friction we're introducing. Hardware isn't just a cost; it's a time sink.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Mizuki, if hardware is such a time sink and we can't find the right people to manage it quickly, it sounds like a double risk. Maybe we should lean toward something leaner?","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,George,,"I agree with Mio. Given the write-off we experienced with a physical-operation business, a leaner, software-based approach seems the most prudent path for our returns.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,May,,"I agree, but we must be careful. If we go with software, we need to ensure it doesn't trigger those massive security review delays Mizuki mentioned, or we'll just be wasting time.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Rin,,Exactly! So we need something that isn't too complex to report and doesn't need a fancy outside appraisal. Simple software sounds like the safest bet for my sanity!,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,It seems we are all converging on a similar conclusion. We need a solution that avoids the pitfalls of physical infrastructure and the delays of high-security data environments.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,Mio,,"I'm glad we're on the same page. Let's keep these constraints in mind—no heavy hardware, no staffing nightmares, and no security bottlenecks—when we finally see the candidates.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,George,,I believe we have a clear set of criteria now. We should prioritize a business model that is scalable without physical overhead and doesn't overextend our current board capacity.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,May,,"I'll be watching the funding requirements closely. If a candidate needs constant capital injections for growth, it's a no from me, regardless of how ""lean"" the software is.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Rin,,I'll be looking for something that keeps our reporting clean and simple. I can't handle another audit that drags on for weeks because of some outside appraisal!,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,I agree. Let's hope the candidates offer a balance of stability and efficiency that doesn't compromise our operational timelines or our sanity.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
