57,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Okay, here are the candidates! We have Fabric Loop, Harvest Sensor, Ledger Bridge, and Clinic Scheduler. Looking at our constraints, Fabric Loop and Harvest Sensor seem too hardware-heavy for us.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,George,,I agree. Fabric Loop's sorting facilities and Harvest Sensor's field instruments align too closely with our previous write-off and the retention issues we've seen. Ledger Bridge seems the most promising.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,May,,"Ledger Bridge looks great for liquidity too. It's a software tool for payment records, so it won't require the heavy physical assets that drain our reserves or fail to secure our credit line.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,1,talk,Rin,,"Ledger Bridge is perfect! It's just software, so no outside appraisals for depots or hardware, and the reporting should be much simpler than the other options.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"I agree. While Clinic Scheduler also avoids hardware, it deals with medical records, which would trigger those long security reviews. Ledger Bridge is the most efficient choice.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Mio,,I'm totally on board with Ledger Bridge. It avoids the staffing headaches of field crews and doesn't seem as risky as the others. Does anyone have any doubts?,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,George,,I have none. It fits our historical success with back-office financial tools and avoids the pitfalls of physical operations. It is the most logical choice for our portfolio.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,May,,"I'm fully convinced. It's lean, it doesn't threaten our liquidity with physical overhead, and it fits the profile of our most successful exits. I'm voting for Ledger Bridge.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Rin,,I'm voting for Ledger Bridge too! It's the only one that doesn't sound like a total headache for our quarter-end reporting. Let's do it!,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,I concur. It avoids the security bottlenecks of medical data and the operational delays of hardware. My vote is also for Ledger Bridge.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Mio,,I'll cast my vote for Ledger Bridge as well! It's the clear winner for all of us.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
